"hadiths[53]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1396,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The riding one should greet the walking one"""
1397,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"""
1398,"the Prophet (ﷺ) said, If the people of the Scripture greet you"""
1399,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""When the Jews greet you, they usually say, 'As-Samu 'alaikum (Death be on you),' so you should say (in reply to them), 'Wa'alaikum (And on you)."""
1400,"A group of Jews came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, As-samu 'Alaika "" (Death be on you) ""1401"",Jabir b. Abdullah reported a hadith like this from Allah's Apostle (ﷺ)"""
1401,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), that he passed by some young boys and greeted them with peace, and said: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it.""
1402"""
1402,"Narrated 'Aishah: Sawdah went out to relieve herself after the (verse regarding) veiling had been revealed. She was a large woman, and could not be hidden from one who knew her. 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saw her and said, ""O Sawdah! By Allah, you cannot hide yourself from us, so think of some way by which you should not be recognized on going out."" Sawdah returned while Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was in my house taking his supper, and there was a bone in his hand. She entered and said, ""O Allah's Messenger! I went out to answer the call of nature and 'Umar said to me so-and-so."" 'Aishah added: Then Allah revealed the Divine Inspiration (relevant to this incident) and then it was over, and the bone was still in his hand as he had not put it down. He then said, ""You (women) have been permitted to go out for your needs."""
1403,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of entering upon women."" A man from the Ansar said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what about Al-Hamw?"" He said: ""Al-Hamw is death.""
1404"""
1404,"Narrated Safiyyah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ): She came to visit the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during his I'tikaf in the mosque, in the last ten days of Ramadan, and she spoke with him for a while, then she got up to return home. The Prophet (ﷺ) got up with her to walk her back, and when she reached the door of the mosque, near the door of Umm Salamah, two men from the Ansar passed by and greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with salam. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to them: ""Wait, this is Safiyyah bint Huyayy."" They said: ""Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah!"" and it was a matter of concern to them. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Satan reaches into man to the extent of his blood (i.e., he is present with him wherever he goes), and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts."""
1405,"A man came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! I am suffering from fatigue and hunger."" The Prophet (ﷺ) sent (somebody) to his wives (to get something) ""1406"",A hadith like this as narrated by Ibn 'Umar has also been transmitted by Abu Sa'id al-Khudri"""
1406,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""A man should not make another man get up from his seat and then sit in it.""
1407"""
1407,"Narrated Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her): The Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon me while a mukhannath (effeminate man) was with me, and he heard him say to 'Abdullah bin Umayyah: ""O 'Abdullah, what do you think, if Allah opens Ta'if for you tomorrow, take the daughter of Ghailan, for she comes forward with four (folds of fat) and turns her back with eight."" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""These should never enter upon you (women)."""
1408,"Narrated Asma' bint Abu Bakr:\n\nWhen Az-Zubair married me, he had no real property or any slave or anything else except a camel \nwhich drew water from the well, and his horse. I used to feed his horse with fodder and drew water \nand sew the bucket for drawing it, and prepare the dough, but I did not know how to bake bread. So \nour Ansari neighbors used to bake bread for me, and they were honorable ladies. I used to carry the \ndate stones on my head from Zubair's land given to him by Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and this land was two third \nFarsakh (about two miles) from my house. One day, while I was coming with the date stones on my \nhead, I met Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) along with some Ansari people. He called me and then, (directing his \ncamel to kneel down) said, \Ikh! Ikh!\"" so as to make me ride behind him (on his camel). I felt shy to \ntravel with the men and remembered Az-Zubair and his sense of Ghira ""1409"",Narrated `Abdullah:\n\nthe Prophet (ﷺ) said \When three persons are together"""
1409,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah said: ""If they are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third.""
1410"""
1410,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""If you are three, then no two of you should whisper together excluding the third person, until you mix with other people, because that will grieve him."""
1411,"Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"""
1412,"Magic was worked on Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) so that he used to think that he had sexual relations with his wives while he actually had not (Sufyan said: That is the hardest kind of magic as it has such an effect). Then one day he said, ""O `Aisha do you know that Allah has instructed me concerning the matter I asked Him about? Two men came to me and one of them sat near my head and the other sat near my feet. The one near my head asked the other. What is wrong with this man?' The latter replied the is under the effect of magic The first one asked, Who has worked magic on him?' The other replied Labid bin Al-A'sam, a man from Bani Zuraiq who was an ally of the Jews and was a hypocrite.' The first one asked, What material did he use)?' The other replied, 'A comb and the hair stuck to it.' The first one asked, 'Where (is that)?' The other replied. 'In a skin of pollen of a male date palm tree kept under a stone in the well of Dharwan' '' So the Prophet (ﷺ) went to that well and took out those things and said ""That was the well which was shown to me (in a dream) Its water looked like the infusion of Henna leaves and its date-palm trees looked like the heads of devils."" The Prophet (ﷺ) added, ""Then that thing was taken out' I said (to the Prophet (ﷺ) ) ""Why do you not treat yourself with Nashra?"" He said, ""Allah has cured me; I dislike to let evil spread among my people."""" ""1413"",Anas reported that a Jewess came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) with poisoned mutton and he took of that what had been brought to him (Allah's Messenger). (When the effect of this poison were felt by him) he called for her and asked her about that"""
1413,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), that a Jewish woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was brought, and it was said: ""Will you not kill her?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""I continued to recognize its effect in the palates of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).""
1414"""
1414,"Narrated 'Aishah: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to visit a sick person, or a sick person was brought to him, he used to say: ""Take away the disease, O Lord of the people, and heal, for You are the Healer. There is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no disease behind."""
1415,"Abdullah reported that Allah's Messenger (may peace be upol him) got fashioned a signet ring of gold but he kept its stone on the inner side of his palm as he wore it, so the people (following his example) got fashioned (such rings). Then one day as he sat on the pulpit he pulled it away saying:I wore this ring and kept its stone towards the inner side. He then threw it away, and said: By Allah, I will never wear it; so the people threw their rings away"""
1416,"Narrated Al-Aswad:\n\nI asked `Aisha about treating poisonous stings (a snake-bite or a scorpion sting) with a Ruqya. She \nsaid, \The Prophet (ﷺ) allowed the treatment of poisonous sting with Ruqya.\"""""""""
1417,"Narrated `Aisha:\n\nOnce the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed on a Khamisa with marks on it and said, \The marks on it diverted my \nattention ""1418"",Narrated `Ali:\n\nAllah's Messenger (ﷺ) ordered me to give in charity the skin and the coverings of the Budn which I had \nslaughtered."""
1418,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, or ordered that Ruqyah be sought for the evil eye.""
1419"""
1419,"Narrated Um Salamah: The Prophet (ﷺ) saw in her house a slave girl who had a black spot on her face, and he said: ""Seek treatment for her by Ruqya, for she is under the effect of an evil eye."""
1420,"We witnessed along with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) the Khaibar (campaign). Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) told his companions about a man who claimed to be a Muslim, This man is from the people of the Fire."" When the battle started"""
1421,"I heard from the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, There will come a time upon the people when the best property of a Muslim will be sheep which he will take to the tops of mountains and to the places of rainfall ""1422"",Abu'l-Bakhtari reported:We saw the new moon of Ramadan as we were at Dhit-i-'Irq. We sent a man to Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with both of them) to ask him (whether the sighting of a small moon had something of the nature of defect in it). Upon this Ibn 'Abbas (Allah be pleased with both of them) said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had said: Verily Allah deferred its sight"""
1422,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hijamah and gave the Hajjam his wage.""
1423"""
1423,"Narrated Anas (رضي الله عنه): The Prophet (ﷺ) used to get himself cupped, and he did not withhold the wages of anyone."
1424,"`Abdullah bin `Umar said, The Prophet (ﷺ) said ""1425"",(the wife of the Prophet) Whenever Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) intended to go on a journey"""
1425,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Asma bint Abi Bakr: She used to, when a woman with a fever was brought to her, supplicate for her, take water and pour it between her and her collar. She said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to cool it with water.""
1426"""
1426,"Narrated Rafi' bin Khadij: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: ""Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."""
1427,"Abu Bakr kissed (the forehead of) the Prophet (ﷺ) when he was dead. `Aisha added: We put medicine in one side of his mouth but he started waving us not to insert the medicine into his mouth. We said, He dislikes the medicine as a patient usually does."" But when he came to his senses he said"""
1428,"Narrated Um Qais bint Mihsin:\n\nI brought my young son, who had not started eating (ordinary food) to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) who took him \nand made him sit in his lap. The child urinated on the garment of the Prophet, so he asked for water \nand poured it over the soiled (area) and did not wash it."""
1429,"I heard the Prophet (ﷺ), Souls are like recruited troops: Those who are like qualities are inclined to each other"""
1430,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, ""There is healing in black cumin for all diseases except death."""" ""1431"",A'isha reported:We took 'Abdullah b. Zubair to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) so that he should put saliva in his mouth and we had to make a good deal of effort in order to procure them"""
1431,"[AI-translation] Hadith of Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a deceased person from her family died, and the women would gather for that, then disperse except for her family and close friends, she would order a pot of Talbinah to be cooked, then Tharid would be made, and the Talbinah would be poured over it. Then she would say: ""Eat from it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Talbinah comforts the heart of the sick and takes away some of the sorrow.'""
1432"""
1432,"Narrated Abu Sa'id: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""My brother has a complaint in his abdomen (i.e. diarrhea)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""Give him honey to drink."" The man came for the second time and the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him, ""Give him honey to drink."" He came for the third time and the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Give him honey to drink."" He returned again and said, ""I have done that (but of no avail)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Allah has said the truth, and your brother's abdomen has told a lie. Give him honey to drink."" So he made him drink it and he became cured."
1433,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Plague was a means of torture sent on a group of Israelis (or on some people before you). So if you hear of its spread in a land"""
1434,"`Umar bin Al-Khattab departed for Sham and when he reached Sargh, the commanders of the (Muslim) army, Abu 'Ubaida bin Al-Jarrah and his companions met him and told him that an epidemic had broken out in Sham. `Umar said, Call for me the early emigrants."" So `Umar called them"""
1435,"This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Zuhri with the same chain of transmitters that be heard Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) as saying on a similar day:I am fasting today, so he who wishes to observe fast should do so; but he did not make mention of the rest of the hadith"""
1436,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: The cattle (sheep, cows, camels, etc.) suffering from a disease should not be mixed up with healthy cattle, (or said: Do not put a patient with a healthy person ). "" (as a precaution)."""""""
1437,"Abu Said al-Khudri reported:'Ali b. Abu Talib sent to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Yemen some gold alloyed with clay in a leather bag dyed in the leaves of Mimosa flava. He distributed it among four men. 'Uyaina b. Hisna, Aqra' b. Habis and Zaid al-Khail, and the fourth one was either Alqama b. 'Ulatha or 'Amir b. Tufail. A person from among his (Prophet's) Companions said: We had a better claim to this (wealth) than these (persons). This (remark) reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) upon which he said: Will you not trust me, whereas I am a trustee of Him Who is in the heaven? The news come to me from the heaven morning and evening. Then there stood up a person with deep sunken eyes, prominent cheek bones, and elevated forehead, thick beard, shaven head, tucked up loincloth, and he said: Messenger of Allah, fear Allah. He (the Holy Prophet) said: Woe to thee. Do I not deserve most to fear Allah amongst the people of the earth? That man then returned. Khalid b. Walid then said: Messenger of Allah, should I not strike his neck? Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: Perhaps he may be observing the prayer. Khalid said: How many observers of prayer are there who profess with their tongue what is not in their heart? Upon this the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: I have not been commanded to pierce through the hearts of people, nor to split their bellies (insides). He again looked at him and he was going back. Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: There would arise a people from the progeny of this (man) who would recite the Qur'an glibly, but it would not go beyond their throats; they would (hurriedly) pass through (the teachings of their) religion just as the arrow passes through the prey. I conceive that he (the Holy Prophet) also said this: If I find them I would certainly kill them as were killed the (people of) Thamud"""
1438,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, The good deeds of any person will not make him enter Paradise."" (i.e. ""1439"",Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"""
1439,"[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""There is no contagion and no bad omen, and ill-luck is in three: in a woman, a house, and a riding beast.""
1440"""
1440,"Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If evil omen is in anything, it is in the woman, the horse and the house."""
1441,"That he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) delivering a sermon on the pulpit saying, ""Kill snakes and kill Dhu-at- Tufyatain (i.e. a snake with two white lines on its back) and Al-Abtar (i.e. a snake with short or mutilated tail) for they destroy the sight of one's eyes and bring about abortion."" (`Abdullah bin `Umar further added): Once while I was chasing a snake in order, to kill it, Abu Lubaba called me saying: ""Don't kill it,"" I said. ""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) ordered us to kill snakes."" He said, ""But later on he prohibited the killing of snakes living in the houses."" (Az-Zuhri said. ""Such snakes are called Al-Awamir."")"""
1442,"While we were with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) in a cave, Surat Wal Mursalat"" was revealed to him and we received it directly from his mouth as soon as he had received the revelation. Suddenly a snake came out and Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said ""1443"",Narrated Um Sharik:\n\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered her to kill Salamanders."""
1443,"[AI-translation] From Umm Sharik, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, ordered her to kill the lizards.""
1444"""
1444,"Narrated 'Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ): That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said regarding the house lizard (gecko), ""It is a wicked little creature,"" but I did not hear him command that it be killed."
1445,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"""
1446,"`Umar asked the people, Who remembers the narration of the Prophet (ﷺ) about the affliction?"" Hudhaifa said"""
1447,"Abu Huraira said, ""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, 'No one should prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."" Abu Huraira said (to his companions), ""Why do I find you averse to it? By Allah, I certainly will narrate it to you."""""""
1448,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""While a dog was going round a well and was about to die of thirst, an Israeli prostitute saw it and took off her shoe and watered it. So Allah forgave her because of that good deed."""""""
